# Ingestion Pipeline

## Corpus

Target: public SaaS help docs (Linear, Stripe, etc.) — ~80–150 articles, clean structure.

## Pipeline steps

1. **parse.ts** — PDF / HTML / MD → plain text with structure preserved.
2. **chunk.ts** — 500–800 tokens, 10–15% overlap; preserve section boundaries when possible.
3. **embed.ts** — Voyage `voyage-3` or OpenAI `text-embedding-3-large`.
4. **run.ts** — CLI entrypoint orchestrating the full pipeline.

## Qdrant metadata (required on every chunk)

```ts
{ source_url, title, section, chunk_index }
```

## Local dev

Qdrant via Docker is acceptable for local dev only — not part of deployed architecture.

## Verification gate (Phase 1)

Before moving to Phase 2, manually run 5–10 hand-picked queries and confirm the right chunks return. Do not skip this eyeball check.
